The real-time trip updates of the subway and the service alerts (GTFS-RT)
are obtained from the servers of the Metropolitan Transportation Authority
(MTA) of the State of New York, https://api.mta.info/, under the MTA terms
and conditions for data feeds:
https://www.mta.info/developers/terms-and-conditions. Each Gladys instance
downloads them on its own server and shows them to its users. The list of the
stations ("MTA Subway Stations") comes from the open data portal of the State
of New York, https://data.ny.gov/d/39hk-dx4f; a copy ships in
src/data/stations.csv. The files under test/fixtures are extracts of these
data.

The data are provided by the MTA "as is": they may not be accurate, complete
or timely, and what the integration shows may not be real time (it reads the
feeds every 30 seconds to 10 minutes).

